## 2. Methodology and Data Sources

This report is generated by **{{ system_name }}** ({{ system_tagline }}) from telemetry
captured by a T-Pot HIVE honeypot deployment consisting of Cowrie (SSH/Telnet), Dionaea
(SMB/malware), Heralding (credential capture), Snare/Tanner (web attacks), Honeytrap
(arbitrary TCP), and FATT (fingerprinting) sensors. Attack telemetry is indexed in an
internal Elasticsearch instance and queried by the {{ system_name }} pipeline. Session-level
events are classified against:

- **[MITRE ATT&CK ↗]({{ '' | mitre_link }})** — attacker technique identification
- **[Lockheed Martin Cyber Kill Chain ↗]({{ '' | kill_chain_link }})** — attack stage classification
- **[NIST Cybersecurity Framework ↗]({{ '' | csf_link }})** — recommendation structuring

Narrative interpretation is provided by a locally-hosted large language model (Llama 3.2
via Ollama). No cloud LLM services are invoked; all raw log data remains on the analyst's
workstation.

